WEBVTT

00:00:07.940 --> 00:00:11.450
A sky without a rainbow feels kinda unusual.

00:00:11.450 --> 00:00:13.580
Homesick already?

00:00:13.580 --> 00:00:14.860
That's not what I meant...

00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:17.110
But over there...

00:00:17.110 --> 00:00:20.270
...the everlasting rainbow you gave me is hanging in the sky.

00:00:22.430 --> 00:00:25.990
Also, I met you in that town.

00:00:25.990 --> 00:00:26.960
What?

00:00:30.560 --> 00:00:34.050
Just thinking how even you could say sappy stuff like that.

00:00:34.330 --> 00:00:35.740
Trying to pick a fight?

00:00:35.740 --> 00:00:37.140
Of course not!

00:00:37.140 --> 00:00:38.220
I'm just happy.

00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:42.240
Let's go see the rainbow again when we get back.

00:00:42.750 --> 00:00:44.800
On top of that hill, together.

00:00:45.610 --> 00:00:46.520
Sure.

00:00:47.070 --> 00:00:51.030
I can't believe I can be like this with you...

00:00:54.240 --> 00:00:55.840
We'll have to get back soon.

00:00:56.450 --> 00:00:57.880
Just a little longer.

00:00:59.140 --> 00:01:00.240
Okay.

00:01:35.490 --> 00:01:38.610
He's coming back tomorrow...

00:01:39.180 --> 00:01:40.390
Haruhiko-kun...

00:01:52.220 --> 00:01:56.140
These feelings that I couldn't even tell my friends about

00:01:57.320 --> 00:02:01.470
are still locked up inside me even now

00:02:02.640 --> 00:02:06.560
If I eat the magical fruit inside my heart

00:02:07.690 --> 00:02:11.530
they might actually be able to come out

00:02:12.780 --> 00:02:17.140
I kept on waiting in the classroom

00:02:18.040 --> 00:02:22.140
making excuses that it's just a coincidence

00:02:22.380 --> 00:02:27.730
That smile is probably meant for someone

00:02:27.730 --> 00:02:33.190
If dreams can make my wishes come true

00:02:33.190 --> 00:02:38.140
I want to give you this present

00:02:38.140 --> 00:02:43.310
I will transform your rainbow

00:02:43.310 --> 00:02:48.270
into a bridge of happiness, just wave to me

00:02:48.480 --> 00:02:53.550
It's all right, it's all right

00:02:53.550 --> 00:02:58.900
I simply want to watch over you...

00:03:11.120 --> 00:03:17.090
<i>Hearts Linked, Feelings Broken</i>

00:03:16.360 --> 00:03:18.510
You two over there!

00:03:18.950 --> 00:03:22.050
If you want a sugary sweet memento, I can recommend this.

00:03:22.050 --> 00:03:23.260
Hey now...

00:03:23.260 --> 00:03:24.650
Black is sweet, smooth bean paste...

00:03:24.650 --> 00:03:26.050
...brown is sweet, rough bean paste...

00:03:26.050 --> 00:03:27.220
...green is green tea flavored bean paste.

00:03:27.570 --> 00:03:31.730
They're very popular souvenirs amongst people who found love on their school trip!

00:03:32.510 --> 00:03:33.680
H-How...?

00:03:33.680 --> 00:03:35.320
We aren't, err...

00:03:35.900 --> 00:03:37.600
What's wrong, Amami?

00:03:38.400 --> 00:03:40.480
Did you catch a fever?

00:03:40.480 --> 00:03:41.980
It's nothing.

00:03:41.980 --> 00:03:43.240
Oh really?

00:03:43.550 --> 00:03:45.870
Did you buy a souvenir yet?

00:03:45.870 --> 00:03:47.200
Of course.

00:03:49.840 --> 00:03:52.420
Seems pretty primitive knowing your tastes.

00:03:52.420 --> 00:03:55.040
Why do you want this, anyway?

00:03:55.040 --> 00:03:56.480
Not very perceptive.

00:03:56.480 --> 00:04:00.100
It's been modded to contain a small-scale electronic brain...

00:04:00.100 --> 00:04:02.270
...and it speaks Kyoto dialect to boot!

00:04:02.270 --> 00:04:04.370
Welcome! Welcome!

00:04:04.370 --> 00:04:06.430
Isn't this the very pinnacle of a Kyoto souvenir?

00:04:06.810 --> 00:04:07.810
Really?

00:04:07.810 --> 00:04:09.960
Welcome! Welcome!

00:04:09.960 --> 00:04:12.690
Moreover, it keeps repeating the same thing...

00:04:12.690 --> 00:04:14.200
How rude.

00:04:14.200 --> 00:04:17.610
It can fire forty ballistic missiles from its belly as well!

00:04:17.610 --> 00:04:18.720
I'll show you.

00:04:19.610 --> 00:04:20.940
Don't!

00:04:24.960 --> 00:04:27.280
Was this really for the best?

00:04:27.560 --> 00:04:31.020
No use buying sweets for that drunkard.

00:04:31.020 --> 00:04:33.010
These pickles should be more than enough.

00:04:33.010 --> 00:04:34.540
I'm not talking about Dad...

00:04:35.330 --> 00:04:36.490
Kirino, huh?

00:04:37.830 --> 00:04:39.380
This should be fine.

00:04:39.780 --> 00:04:41.540
These are perfectly normal Kyoto souvenirs.

00:04:42.240 --> 00:04:45.380
But she wanted that charm...

00:04:45.740 --> 00:04:48.130
I can't exactly do that, can I?

00:04:49.680 --> 00:04:51.960
I'll let Kirino know.

00:04:51.960 --> 00:04:53.750
About us?

00:04:53.750 --> 00:04:54.810
Yeah.

00:04:55.310 --> 00:04:58.240
What will she think?

00:04:58.240 --> 00:04:59.870
Are you regretting it?

00:04:59.870 --> 00:05:00.820
No.

00:05:01.700 --> 00:05:03.570
I just feel a little uneasy.

00:05:03.570 --> 00:05:06.470
It's all right. I'm with you.

00:05:17.410 --> 00:05:18.820
Heavy!

00:05:18.820 --> 00:05:21.570
Do your best, it's just a little further!

00:05:21.570 --> 00:05:23.960
I'm supposed to be used to traveling...

00:05:23.960 --> 00:05:26.970
I suddenly got tired the moment we returned.

00:05:26.970 --> 00:05:30.470
Returning to your home turf makes your stress dissolve.

00:05:30.470 --> 00:05:32.340
Were you stressed?

00:05:32.340 --> 00:05:34.220
Well, a lot of things have happened.

00:05:35.900 --> 00:05:36.850
You're right.

00:05:37.230 --> 00:05:38.700
What?

00:05:38.700 --> 00:05:41.800
Hey, can we link arms?

00:05:41.800 --> 00:05:43.860
While we're struggling with our luggage?

00:05:44.160 --> 00:05:46.610
It'll be fine, we can do it!

00:05:46.610 --> 00:05:48.060
Well, I don't mind.

00:05:53.520 --> 00:05:55.660
When did you become such a spoiled girl?

00:05:55.660 --> 00:05:59.170
We weren't alone on our trip home.

00:05:59.620 --> 00:06:03.160
Your breasts are pretty big after all.

00:06:03.160 --> 00:06:05.670
No need to point that out!

00:06:07.850 --> 00:06:09.700
<i>I've obviously been cautious...</i>

00:06:10.290 --> 00:06:12.780
<i>...but in my bliss, it never even crossed my mind.</i>

00:06:13.600 --> 00:06:15.540
<i>That things would turn out like this...</i>

00:06:29.990 --> 00:06:31.520
Come on, let's go.

00:06:38.640 --> 00:06:39.520
I'm home.

00:06:40.000 --> 00:06:41.360
Welcome back.

00:06:42.310 --> 00:06:43.400
I'm home...

00:06:47.820 --> 00:06:48.990
Have you been well?

00:06:50.420 --> 00:06:52.180
I see, that's good.

00:06:53.240 --> 00:06:55.600
I bought you a souvenir!

00:06:55.600 --> 00:06:58.120
A genuine Hokkaido-made stuffed bear!

00:06:58.750 --> 00:06:59.690
Thanks...

00:07:01.630 --> 00:07:03.980
Actually, it's just yatsuhashi.

00:07:03.980 --> 00:07:06.360
Let's head inside for now.

00:07:06.670 --> 00:07:09.670
No, right here is fine.

00:07:09.670 --> 00:07:10.680
Okay...

00:07:11.830 --> 00:07:13.370
Haruhiko-kun...

00:07:13.820 --> 00:07:18.370
...you're only giving me a normal souvenir, huh.

00:07:19.370 --> 00:07:20.660
I'm sorry.

00:07:21.520 --> 00:07:24.490
There's a temple that is famed to be able to fulfill one's love.

00:07:24.490 --> 00:07:25.210
Do you know it?

00:07:27.030 --> 00:07:29.220
I want a charm from there.

00:07:30.020 --> 00:07:32.630
One from you, to me!

00:07:33.330 --> 00:07:34.500
I...

00:07:34.500 --> 00:07:36.510
...can't give you the charm.

00:07:37.830 --> 00:07:39.960
The girl I love is Riko.

00:07:44.450 --> 00:07:45.890
I see...

00:07:47.090 --> 00:07:48.860
...just like I thought.

00:07:48.860 --> 00:07:50.030
You knew, didn't you?

00:07:51.950 --> 00:07:53.800
Did Riko-chan confess?

00:07:53.800 --> 00:07:55.580
I confessed to her.

00:07:55.580 --> 00:07:57.650
I see...

00:08:07.460 --> 00:08:08.950
Congrats!

00:08:08.950 --> 00:08:10.040
Kirino...

00:08:10.560 --> 00:08:12.780
Isn't that great, Riko-chan?

00:08:12.780 --> 00:08:14.020
Sorry.

00:08:14.020 --> 00:08:16.400
No, it's all right.

00:08:16.400 --> 00:08:19.650
I like Haruhiko-kun.

00:08:19.650 --> 00:08:21.350
And I like you too.

00:08:21.350 --> 00:08:22.480
That's why...

00:08:22.880 --> 00:08:24.010
That's why...

00:08:28.100 --> 00:08:29.480
That's why it's fine!

00:08:29.990 --> 00:08:31.300
Kirino-chan...

00:08:32.440 --> 00:08:33.990
Thanks for the souvenir.

00:08:34.810 --> 00:08:36.040
Kirino!

00:08:36.040 --> 00:08:37.560
See you at school!

00:08:39.450 --> 00:08:41.010
Onii-chan...

00:08:41.010 --> 00:08:42.610
Is this really okay?

00:08:42.610 --> 00:08:43.560
Yeah...

00:08:44.060 --> 00:08:45.420
It is, right?

00:08:45.420 --> 00:08:46.500
Yeah.

00:09:08.990 --> 00:09:10.840
Sorry it was take-out.

00:09:10.840 --> 00:09:13.560
It's fine. I'm sure you were tired today.

00:09:14.190 --> 00:09:17.990
He went on a business trip the very day we come back...

00:09:17.990 --> 00:09:20.690
Dad is very busy.

00:09:20.690 --> 00:09:23.020
This might be for the best though.

00:09:23.020 --> 00:09:25.620
He'd be shocked to see us all over each other.

00:09:26.450 --> 00:09:27.500
Are you going to tell him?

00:09:28.090 --> 00:09:32.130
No need to go out of our way to hide it, or tell him for that matter.

00:09:32.130 --> 00:09:34.560
He'll learn about it eventually.

00:09:35.300 --> 00:09:37.830
We should just keep on living the way we used to.

00:09:37.830 --> 00:09:38.550
Right?

00:09:38.550 --> 00:09:39.840
Okay.

00:09:39.840 --> 00:09:41.810
I guess I'll go take a bath.

00:09:41.810 --> 00:09:42.850
Onii-chan.

00:09:44.270 --> 00:09:46.440
Stay with me from now on, okay?

00:09:46.910 --> 00:09:47.980
Of course.

00:09:48.710 --> 00:09:50.190
It's a promise.

00:09:50.190 --> 00:09:50.960
Yeah.

00:09:59.130 --> 00:10:01.070
It's brighter than usual.

00:10:05.750 --> 00:10:06.840
Hello?

00:10:12.070 --> 00:10:13.070
Hello?

00:10:17.940 --> 00:10:18.890
Hello?

00:10:19.780 --> 00:10:20.800
Hello?

00:10:21.420 --> 00:10:22.380
Hello?

00:10:22.840 --> 00:10:23.970
Hello?

00:10:24.470 --> 00:10:27.030
Hello?

00:10:31.490 --> 00:10:34.020
Open your eyes! Hyper kick!

00:10:36.170 --> 00:10:38.490
I like a hot-blooded youth like you!

00:10:38.860 --> 00:10:40.510
Wake up, Onii-chan.

00:10:44.360 --> 00:10:46.500
Good morning, Onii-chan.

00:10:47.140 --> 00:10:48.520
Ah, good mor—

00:10:50.210 --> 00:10:51.540
You didn't...

00:10:51.540 --> 00:10:52.970
Of course not!

00:10:52.970 --> 00:10:54.100
Geez.

00:10:54.100 --> 00:10:56.260
You just don't give away any freebies, do you?

00:10:57.140 --> 00:10:59.890
If I did that, their worth would fade.

00:11:01.860 --> 00:11:03.530
Oh really?

00:11:03.530 --> 00:11:04.560
Yes, really.

00:11:05.710 --> 00:11:08.440
But here's an indirect kiss.

00:11:11.470 --> 00:11:13.810
Why are you waking me this early anyway?

00:11:14.160 --> 00:11:17.690
Don't you know we're free the day after our school trip?

00:11:17.690 --> 00:11:19.820
I want to go somewhere.

00:11:28.780 --> 00:11:31.140
This is where you wanted to go?

00:11:31.140 --> 00:11:31.890
Yup.

00:11:36.340 --> 00:11:38.440
An eternal rainbow, huh?

00:11:38.440 --> 00:11:43.270
I had no idea it was a Gift from you, though.

00:11:43.920 --> 00:11:46.050
Hey, Onii-chan, do you remember?

00:11:46.770 --> 00:11:50.210
We watched the rainbow from this place in the past, didn't we?

00:11:50.210 --> 00:11:50.850
Yeah.

00:11:50.850 --> 00:11:52.850
So pretty!

00:11:53.320 --> 00:11:56.680
Here's where you can see the rainbow the biggest!

00:12:00.580 --> 00:12:02.400
It's disappearing...

00:12:02.930 --> 00:12:05.360
Let's go see the rainbow here again someday.

00:12:05.360 --> 00:12:07.450
I'll take you along.

00:12:08.710 --> 00:12:09.740
Okay!

00:12:10.750 --> 00:12:15.210
The reason I decided to send the rainbow was because of that promise.

00:12:15.600 --> 00:12:21.280
The promise to go see the rainbow again the next time one appeared.

00:12:21.280 --> 00:12:24.220
But that opportunity never came around.

00:12:25.810 --> 00:12:28.280
That's why I decided to send a rainbow.

00:12:28.280 --> 00:12:33.230
So that we could be together forever, as long as we could gaze at that rainbow.

00:12:33.600 --> 00:12:38.850
So that you would be reminded I was here whenever you looked up at it.

00:12:39.540 --> 00:12:40.910
I see.

00:12:40.910 --> 00:12:43.650
What happened in the past doesn't really matter, though.

00:12:44.450 --> 00:12:45.910
Because...

00:12:45.910 --> 00:12:49.070
...we've become lovers now.

00:12:49.070 --> 00:12:49.970
Riko...

00:12:51.200 --> 00:12:53.790
You want to kiss me again, don't you?

00:12:53.790 --> 00:12:55.120
I... err...

00:13:02.550 --> 00:13:05.640
I had always regretted it.

00:13:05.640 --> 00:13:06.820
What?

00:13:06.820 --> 00:13:08.460
Sending the Gift.

00:13:09.130 --> 00:13:10.150
Why?

00:13:10.150 --> 00:13:12.060
I couldn't forgive myself.

00:13:13.750 --> 00:13:18.020
Well... I'm sure you know all about it...

00:13:18.020 --> 00:13:19.570
My bad habit.

00:13:20.780 --> 00:13:22.570
Fawning on others, you mean?

00:13:23.690 --> 00:13:26.420
I hated that part of me as well.

00:13:27.110 --> 00:13:33.070
In particular, I didn't want to behave like that towards you.

00:13:33.070 --> 00:13:36.780
You're the person I love, after all.

00:13:37.420 --> 00:13:38.590
Riko...

00:13:38.590 --> 00:13:39.930
That is the reason.

00:13:40.630 --> 00:13:45.200
I believed Gift to be something used just to get someone to like you.

00:13:46.280 --> 00:13:49.200
Gift is a magical power, after all.

00:13:49.200 --> 00:13:51.010
Stronger than any present...

00:13:51.450 --> 00:13:54.020
...it makes it possible to seize someone's love, right?

00:13:54.020 --> 00:13:57.460
I... guess that can happen as well.

00:13:57.460 --> 00:14:00.290
But you know, Gift requires both parties to feel...

00:14:02.730 --> 00:14:04.970
To the person you love...

00:14:04.970 --> 00:14:08.240
To send a damn Gift to the person you hold most dearly, of all people...

00:14:09.710 --> 00:14:11.940
"A damn Gift," huh?

00:14:11.940 --> 00:14:13.990
That's why I've always regretted it.

00:14:14.340 --> 00:14:16.540
I wanted that rainbow to just disappear.

00:14:18.170 --> 00:14:19.430
But you know...

00:14:19.890 --> 00:14:21.430
I feel differently now.

00:14:21.430 --> 00:14:23.560
I finally understood.

00:14:23.560 --> 00:14:24.380
What?

00:14:24.380 --> 00:14:28.970
If that Gift had really brought forth my one-sided feelings...

00:14:29.590 --> 00:14:31.160
...I think it would've gotten deflected.

00:14:31.910 --> 00:14:33.890
Just like the incidents before.

00:14:35.010 --> 00:14:36.510
But that wasn't the case.

00:14:36.510 --> 00:14:40.000
The rainbow has always been there, and is still shining brightly.

00:14:40.000 --> 00:14:41.310
I see.

00:14:41.680 --> 00:14:45.640
We both wished to go see the rainbow together again.

00:14:45.640 --> 00:14:47.530
We felt the same way.

00:14:47.530 --> 00:14:49.570
It was properly received.

00:14:49.570 --> 00:14:50.470
Yeah.

00:14:51.000 --> 00:14:53.500
That's why that rainbow won't disappear.

00:14:53.500 --> 00:14:55.800
As long as we're together...

00:14:55.800 --> 00:14:56.560
Yeah.

00:14:58.590 --> 00:15:01.460
No matter how many years pass...

00:15:01.460 --> 00:15:03.460
...let's go see the rainbow again.

00:15:04.030 --> 00:15:05.340
Just the two of us.

00:15:25.270 --> 00:15:30.030
<i>I'm the one who has always been together with Haruhiko-kun!</i>

00:15:30.630 --> 00:15:32.870
<i>I thought I'd be with him forever.</i>

00:15:33.290 --> 00:15:36.500
<i>Then Riko-chan intruded between the two of us.</i>

00:15:37.460 --> 00:15:40.230
<i>My place slowly began to disappear.</i>

00:15:41.070 --> 00:15:43.430
<i>Even though I want to be by Haruhiko-kun's side...</i>

00:15:44.460 --> 00:15:49.210
<i>...my place is gradually being stolen away by Riko-chan!</i>

00:15:58.590 --> 00:16:03.850
<i>If I don't do anything now, I won't be able to be with Haruhiko-kun ever again!</i>

00:16:07.000 --> 00:16:08.180
<i>No.</i>

00:16:08.180 --> 00:16:09.340
<i>No!</i>

00:16:09.340 --> 00:16:10.490
<i>No!!!</i>

00:16:12.490 --> 00:16:15.680
<i>I want to be by Haruhiko-kun's side...</i>

00:16:26.280 --> 00:16:28.270
Kirino... what's up?

00:16:29.880 --> 00:16:32.130
Nothing in particular...

00:16:34.130 --> 00:16:38.290
Riko went to pick up some vegetables at Tama-nee's place.

00:16:38.290 --> 00:16:40.140
I see.

00:16:40.140 --> 00:16:43.480
I wanted to talk to you for a bit.

00:16:44.150 --> 00:16:44.980
Come in.

00:16:46.050 --> 00:16:47.980
Sorry about yesterday.

00:16:48.680 --> 00:16:51.450
I overreacted a little.

00:16:51.450 --> 00:16:54.650
It's understandable. I'm sorry about that.

00:16:54.650 --> 00:16:56.510
Don't apologize.

00:16:56.510 --> 00:16:58.370
I'm not mad at you.

00:16:58.670 --> 00:17:00.340
Actually, I'm glad.

00:17:01.320 --> 00:17:04.820
You and Riko-chan make a great match.

00:17:05.330 --> 00:17:07.130
I've always felt that way.

00:17:07.130 --> 00:17:08.870
R-Really?

00:17:08.870 --> 00:17:09.860
Yup.

00:17:09.860 --> 00:17:14.430
That's why I want us to stay friends.

00:17:16.040 --> 00:17:18.550
I don't want our friendship to fall apart.

00:17:18.550 --> 00:17:20.460
You don't mind, do you?

00:17:20.460 --> 00:17:25.120
Well, if you're okay with it, we don't mind at all.

00:17:25.120 --> 00:17:26.610
Great!

00:17:26.610 --> 00:17:29.610
I don't want you to dislike me.

00:17:29.930 --> 00:17:31.000
I see.

00:17:32.330 --> 00:17:35.110
So, what have you been doing today?

00:17:35.610 --> 00:17:37.660
Me and Riko went to see the rainbow.

00:17:37.660 --> 00:17:38.810
The rainbow?

00:17:38.810 --> 00:17:39.750
Yeah.

00:17:39.750 --> 00:17:41.740
The rainbow Riko sent.

00:17:44.280 --> 00:17:45.970
You didn't know, did you?

00:17:45.970 --> 00:17:47.500
It surprised me as well.

00:17:47.930 --> 00:17:52.210
That eternal rainbow turned out to be a Gift from Riko.

00:17:52.210 --> 00:17:53.260
A Gift...

00:17:54.080 --> 00:17:55.260
...from Riko?

00:17:55.260 --> 00:17:57.230
I was shocked!

00:17:57.230 --> 00:17:59.760
Who'd have ever thought Riko was responsible for it?

00:18:00.040 --> 00:18:03.820
In the past, we went to see a rainbow once.

00:18:03.820 --> 00:18:06.130
At that time, we made a promise to...

00:18:06.840 --> 00:18:07.770
Kirino?

00:18:08.310 --> 00:18:10.770
Riko-chan used a Gift?

00:18:10.770 --> 00:18:12.450
Hey, Kirino?

00:18:13.680 --> 00:18:14.780
I'm home!

00:18:21.240 --> 00:18:22.990
Kirino-chan...

00:18:22.990 --> 00:18:24.100
Why...

00:18:24.670 --> 00:18:26.240
...did you break our promise?

00:18:29.440 --> 00:18:30.570
Your promise?

00:18:31.150 --> 00:18:33.550
Why did you use a Gift?

00:18:33.550 --> 00:18:35.260
What about our promise!?

00:18:38.720 --> 00:18:40.220
That's not fair, Riko-chan!

00:18:40.620 --> 00:18:42.770
Just what is this promise?

00:18:42.770 --> 00:18:44.970
A promise not to use any Gifts.

00:18:48.450 --> 00:18:49.960
You too, Kirino-chan?

00:18:49.960 --> 00:18:52.440
Yeah, I love Haruhiko-kun!

00:18:52.880 --> 00:18:54.190
You too, don't you?

00:18:55.180 --> 00:18:56.190
Yeah...

00:18:56.190 --> 00:18:57.910
What should we do?

00:18:57.910 --> 00:19:01.740
We can't both be his girlfriend...

00:19:02.140 --> 00:19:03.310
We're rivals?

00:19:03.310 --> 00:19:05.120
I guess that's how it is.

00:19:05.730 --> 00:19:08.280
Then how about we make a promise?

00:19:08.280 --> 00:19:09.790
A promise?

00:19:09.790 --> 00:19:11.750
A promise not to use a Gift.

00:19:11.750 --> 00:19:13.950
It's not fair to use that, is it?

00:19:15.570 --> 00:19:19.510
You can use it for something else, just not for Onii-chan.

00:19:19.510 --> 00:19:20.490
How about it?

00:19:20.490 --> 00:19:21.360
Okay!

00:19:21.360 --> 00:19:22.560
I understand!

00:19:22.560 --> 00:19:23.390
It's a promise!

00:19:23.760 --> 00:19:25.390
It's our promise!

00:19:28.060 --> 00:19:29.970
You two promised something like that...

00:19:31.030 --> 00:19:32.750
And yet, Riko-chan has...

00:19:34.180 --> 00:19:35.200
I'm sorry...

00:19:35.740 --> 00:19:37.190
But listen to me.

00:19:37.190 --> 00:19:40.360
At that time, I thought I'd never see Onii-chan again.

00:19:40.360 --> 00:19:43.370
That's why I wanted him to at least remember me...

00:19:43.970 --> 00:19:47.520
Because I thought I might never see him again.

00:19:48.330 --> 00:19:49.720
That's why...

00:19:49.720 --> 00:19:51.910
Then why did you come back!?

00:19:52.800 --> 00:19:58.380
When you left, I thought Haruhiko-kun would finally pay attention to me again.

00:19:59.080 --> 00:20:00.420
Kirino-chan...

00:20:00.880 --> 00:20:02.570
I...

00:20:02.570 --> 00:20:05.250
I thought I had finally become his little sister...

00:20:06.190 --> 00:20:07.890
Why did you have to come back!?

00:20:11.690 --> 00:20:13.340
My little sister...?

00:20:13.340 --> 00:20:15.080
Kirino, you...

00:20:15.080 --> 00:20:19.860
I always wanted to become your little sister.

00:20:20.860 --> 00:20:22.770
I love you...

00:20:23.660 --> 00:20:25.910
...so I want to be with you forever.

00:20:26.200 --> 00:20:28.550
Being just a childhood friend gives me no certainties...

00:20:28.550 --> 00:20:30.280
...but a little sister...

00:20:30.280 --> 00:20:32.030
...is forever a little sister, right?

00:20:32.640 --> 00:20:34.420
That's what I believed...

00:20:34.420 --> 00:20:38.090
But then Riko-chan came, and became your little sister.

00:20:38.090 --> 00:20:40.830
And when I had finally taken back that dream...

00:20:41.320 --> 00:20:43.130
...she's come to take it away again!

00:20:43.130 --> 00:20:46.600
Why do you keep stealing away my dream!?

00:20:50.600 --> 00:20:52.880
It's... not like that...

00:20:52.880 --> 00:20:54.080
I...

00:20:54.080 --> 00:20:55.730
Even using a Gift...

00:20:59.680 --> 00:21:00.810
I'm sorry...

00:21:02.220 --> 00:21:05.260
It's dirty, Riko-chan!

00:21:05.260 --> 00:21:06.680
I'm sorry...

00:21:06.680 --> 00:21:07.820
I'm so sorry...

00:21:07.820 --> 00:21:09.340
Wait, Kirino!

00:21:09.340 --> 00:21:10.870
Riko's Gift has nothing to do with it!

00:21:11.290 --> 00:21:12.780
I've always loved Riko...

00:21:12.780 --> 00:21:13.870
I've heard enough!

00:21:15.660 --> 00:21:16.170
Kirino!

00:21:19.380 --> 00:21:20.300
Kirino...

00:21:20.900 --> 00:21:22.340
It's okay.

00:21:24.430 --> 00:21:27.340
I haven't given up yet.

00:21:27.850 --> 00:21:30.310
I still have my Gift!

00:21:30.920 --> 00:21:32.100
Kirino-chan...

00:22:12.170 --> 00:22:16.350
In a corner of the classroom

00:22:17.240 --> 00:22:22.940
I hummed my favourite song

00:22:23.760 --> 00:22:28.870
Why did those melancholic feelings

00:22:29.910 --> 00:22:33.100
well up within me today

00:22:34.650 --> 00:22:40.140
When I return, will this town

00:22:40.140 --> 00:22:43.930
gently welcome me back?

00:22:43.930 --> 00:22:48.120
Hey, I want to meet you

00:22:49.680 --> 00:22:55.240
In times you feel down, I wish you would tell me

00:22:55.240 --> 00:23:00.160
before you can no longer turn back

00:23:01.230 --> 00:23:04.110
Building a heartfelt rainbow together

00:23:04.110 --> 00:23:06.920
Say that I'm not alone

00:23:06.920 --> 00:23:12.990
So that my prayers may be heard

00:23:31.350 --> 00:23:32.390
Gift.

00:23:32.390 --> 00:23:35.680
The mysterious power that gives happiness to the people.

00:23:35.680 --> 00:23:38.520
It can make any unfulfilled dream come true.

00:23:39.600 --> 00:23:43.020
It will make this little dream of mine come true, won't it?

00:23:43.530 --> 00:23:46.580
I'll give the future Haruhiko-kun to Riko-chan.

00:23:46.580 --> 00:23:50.070
So let me have the Haruhiko-kun up until now!

00:23:49.960 --> 00:23:59.870
<i>A Past Taken Away</i>

00:23:51.170 --> 00:23:53.600
Next time, "A Past Taken Away."

00:23:54.500 --> 00:23:57.620
Gift. Please make my wish come true!
